    "text": "<p>A rod of length&nbsp;<math><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">l</mtext></mrow></math> (laterally thermally insulated) of the uniform cross-sectional area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;consists of a material whose thermal conductivity varies with temperature as <math> <mrow> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">K</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">K</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">a</mtext> <mo>+</mo> <mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">bT</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;are constants. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> are the temperatures of two ends of the rod. Then, the rate of flow of heat across the rod is</p>\r",
